{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause confirmed — the gate measures the ticket store, not the code checkout\n\nInvestigation reproduced CI locally within pack-transfer variance: **648,346 KiB** local against Actions' **648,505 KiB**.\n\n### The pack is not the code\n\n| Fetch shape | size-pack KiB | Share of failing pack |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| main-only, blobless, full history | 23,268 | 3.6% |\n| tickets-only, blobless, full history | 624,881 | 96.4% |\n| all-heads, blobless, full history | 648,346 | 100% (reproduces CI) |\n\n`.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` checks out with `filter: blob:none` and `fetch-depth: 0`. The unbounded depth pulls every remote head, including `origin/tickets`. The authorship gate then measures that combined pack and fails closed.\n\nComposition of the failing pack by object type:\n\n```\nblob    count=5098    disk_kib=24605.6     3.8%\ncommit  count=296468  disk_kib=56059.5     8.6%\ntree    count=518053  disk_kib=553579.0   85.4%\n```\n\nTree objects are 85.4% of it, and the tickets-only blobless fetch contains **zero blobs**. This is the event-sourced ticket store's directory graph, which is exactly what an append-only store accumulates.\n\n### It is not a large file, and not organic growth\n\nThe four largest blobs across all heads total roughly 1.7 MiB; all blobs together are 24.0 MiB. No single-artifact removal can address an 85 MiB overage. The top 30 ticket tree objects are 9,514 KiB — 1.47% of the pack. The cost is the accumulation of 494,742 tree objects, not any one object.\n\n### The crossing was a discrete history event, not a growth curve\n\n| Point | size-pack KiB |\n|---|---:|\n| 2026-09-04 | 482,385 |\n| 2026-09-09 | 496,077 |\n| 2026-09-10 18:30Z | 496,938 |\n| **2026-09-10 19:00Z** | **598,124** |\n| 2026-09-17 12:57Z | 624,751 |\n\nBaseline growth is ~2.5 MiB/day before and ~3.9 MiB/day after. Between 18:30Z and 19:00Z on 2026-09-10 the pack gained **101,186 KiB in about 30 minutes**. The commit at the jump, `924a93f21edf6c4066339feeb7fff2294244d917` (`chore: sync events from rebar reconciler [run 34514936676]`), is not a descendant of the commit before it and makes **28,570 previously-unreachable commits** reachable, the oldest dating to 2026-08-29.\n\nThis matters for the fix: extrapolating a new limit from a growth rate would be fitting a line to a step.\n\n### This repository already learned this lesson\n\nThe Gerrit-side workflow carries an explicit note against the very gate that is failing here:\n\n```\nNOTE: there is deliberately NO pack-size gate here. A hard cap on the tickets\npack ... is guaranteed to be crossed eventually and, once crossed, casts Verified -1\non EVERY Gerrit change repo-wide until someone bumps the number.\n```\n\nThe scheduled authorship gate has the same property, differing only in blast radius. `d0bcd620278` already raised this limit once from 102400 to 563200 and described it as a temporary bridge; the comment still says to restore 102400. That is the second crossing of a cap whose input is an append-only store, which is the predicted behaviour rather than a surprise.\n\nThe limit is not single-sourced in a `.github/*-limit.txt` file. It lives in the workflow and is mirrored by a contract test at `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py:101`, so any change must move both.\n\n### Not done, and deliberately so\n\nThe reconciler behaviour that made run `34514936676` introduce 28,570 older commits non-linearly was not traced to source. The Git evidence establishes the event and its pack impact; the code path did not get read. Filed separately so it is not lost inside this gate fix.\n\nNo `git gc`, `repack`, `prune`, or `fsck` was run. All measurements come from fresh scratch clones.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789672467583695284,"uuid":"8511115d-71b0-4156-8755-04e18de3c785"}